cvcpkg: no mutable process-wide state in CDT's headers.

libcvc keeps no mutable process-wide state (all state lives in objects the caller
owns), and checks that by scanning object files for writable data. Two things in
CDT 2.0.1's headers show up there:

- Triangulation.hpp: detail::log2_bc's `static double log2_constant` is never
  written; it becomes `static const`. (It is compiled only before C++11.)
- predicates.h (William Lenthe's predicates): Epsilon<T>()'s static,
  ExpansionBase<T>::Splitter and the Constants<T> error bounds are `const`, but
  their initialisers call std::exp2 or a function, so every object file got
  writable copies and guard variables. They are initialised from constant
  expressions now (numeric_limits<T>::epsilon() / 2, 1ULL << (digits / 2 + 1)),
  with the same values. The pre-C++11 path is unchanged.

Not reported upstream yet.

--- a/CDT/include/Triangulation.hpp
+++ b/CDT/include/Triangulation.hpp
@@ -2334,7 +2334,7 @@
 #ifdef CDT_CXX11_IS_SUPPORTED
     return std::log2(x);
 #else
-    static double log2_constant = std::log(2.0);
+    static const double log2_constant = std::log(2.0);
     return std::log(static_cast<double>(x)) / log2_constant;
 #endif
 }
--- a/CDT/include/predicates.h
